 placement exam (administered by faculty)<br>\n\t\t </li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li><a href=\"#\" class=\"permalink\" data-permalink_id=\"None\" data-legacy_id=\"225\" data-signature=\"026141cd39ef1cba4c83855fea5757de\" data-display_type=\"tooltip\" data-link_text=\"%prefix% %code%\" data-anchor_text=\"\" data-from_id=\"None\" data-from_type=\"core\" data-to_id=\"0\" data-to_type=\"unlinked\" data-show_title=\"1\"></a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"permalink\" data-permalink_id=\"None\" data-legacy_id=\"226\" data-signature=\"0a7d07138b37a4b44881edc4091b1c2d\" data-display_type=\"tooltip\" data-link_text=\"%prefix% %code%\" data-anchor_text=\"\" data-from_id=\"None\" data-from_type=\"core\" data-to_id=\"0\" data-to_type=\"unlinked\" data-show_title=\"1\"></a> </li>\n</ul>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p><strong>Requirements of the Major:</strong></p>\n\n<p>A major in Computer Science consists of 10 courses: 8 computer science courses (three core courses and five electives) and two mathematics courses. Of the five electives, at least one must come from Systems and at least one must come from Applications. The other three electives are unrestricted. MAT 230 and CSC 221 should be completed before spring of the junior year.</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><strong>Mathematics Courses:</strong>\n\n\t<ul>\n\t\t<li><a href=\"#\" class=\"permalink\" data-permalink_id=\"None\" data-legacy_id=\"227\" data-signature=\"04febbdecc3f6b2fcfc0917c72fc903f\" data-display_type=\"tooltip\" data-link_text=\"%prefix% %code%\" data-anchor_text=\"\" data-from_id=\"None\" data-from_type=\"core\" data-to_id=\"0\" data-to_type=\"unlinked\" data-show_title=\"1\"></a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"permalink\" data-permalink_id=\"None\" data-legacy_id=\"228\" data-signature=\"e25d7fcb0d5ff933b373029e454f1d44\" data-display_type=\"tooltip\" data-link_text=\"%prefix% %code%\" data-anchor_text=\"\" data-from_id=\"None\" data-from_type=\"core\" data-to_id=\"0\" data-to_type=\"unlinked\" data-show_title=\"1\"></a> </li>\n\t\t<li><a href=